{"type":"after","callId":"call@266","endTime":50173.467,"result":{"value":{"s":"\n    Home/Manual/Developer reference/$WEAP — the weapon definition\n    \n\n — the weapon definition\nForty-odd comma-separated tokens that make a weapon out of data: damage, cadence, fire mode, ammo, sounds, IR type\n✅bench🔍appLast verified 2026-08-27View as Markdown\nWhat the badges mean✅bench Verified on our bench📖official Official Battle Company docs🔍app Decoded from the Callsign app👥community Community-reported🧪software Built + software-tested📐spec Specified only🚧under construction Under constructionNothing unconfirmed is published — see Credits & sourcing.\n\nA weapon is data, not firmware.The gun has no weapons baked in; the host sends a full  frame into one of six slots (0–5). The field names come from the Callsign app's metadata (declaration order = wire order); the positions and meanings below were then pinned by capturing twenty stock weapons with the operator naming each one, and by flipping single tokens on a live gun.Source: protocol/callsign-extract/protocol-classes.md (WEAP), protocol/brx-protocol.md §6, §6.1\n\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md §6; mcp/brx_mcp/__main__.py (captured frames)\nDEV-05diagram pendingToken ruler t0–t42 colour-coded by block: identity · damage/IR · secondary (dormant) · extra-headset · cadence/ammo · fire mode/overheat · sounds · tail.Source: table below\nToken map (0-indexed: ; the slot is t0)39 rows\n\n\ntok\nField\nAR\nCharge Rifle\nMeaning\nConf\n\n\n\n0\nslot\n0\n1\nWeapon slot 0–5. Slot 4 = melee by convention (gyro swing, ).\n✅bench\n\n\n1\nslotType / mode flag\n—\n—\n on exactly the three weapons carrying an extra-headset payload (t12/t13/t42 populated);  on melee;  rail gun; empty otherwise. Not fire mode.\n✅bench\n\n\n2\n—\n100\n100\n— (unknown)\n—\n\n\n3\nprimaryDamageType\n0\n8\nThe IR word's B field /  protocol key. Writing a type here is echoed by the victim in  token 2 and selects its  row. DamageType enum: 0 Standard · 1 MedicHeal · 2 ActivateShield · 3 RallyPulse · 4 Radiation · 5 Cryogenic · 6 ArmorPiercing · 7 EMP · 8 Shrapnel · 9 StickyBomb · 10 StandardLethalExplosive · 11 NonLethalExplosive · 12 ShottyPellets · 13 MeleeDamage · 14 Plasma. Stock: 8 charge, 10 rocket, 11 gas, 13 melee.\n✅bench (position) 🔍app (enum names)\n\n\n4\nprimaryPowerType\n0\n0\nIRSource enum: DeviceCommand, IRSource, GunLaser, HeadSetOnly, GunAndHead, DoubleGun, DoubleGunAndHead, DRY_FIRE, MuzzleFlash, MuzOnly, VibOnly, MuzAndVib. Order relative to t3 was settled by t3 behaving as damageType.\n🔍app\n\n\n5\nprimaryDamage\n24\n150\nThe raw magnitude put in the IR word (=  token 5). Applied damage depends on the victim's  row. The stock AR actually emits 9; the sample's 24 is the manual's stale anchor.\n✅bench\n\n\n6\nprimaryCriticalChance\n0\n0\nCrit chance. 0 on every stock weapon; the IR crit bit can be set (×1.5).\n🔍app\n\n\n7–11\nsecondaryFireChance, secondaryDamageType, secondaryPowerType, secondaryDamage, secondaryCriticalChance\n—\n—\nDormant: empty on all 20 stock weapons. No stock BRX weapon has a secondary fire mode.\n🔍app\n\n\n12\nextraHeadsetDamage\n—\n—\nPopulated with t1=2: Shotgun 70, Rocket 115, Plasma Sniper 80.\n✅bench (correlation)\n\n\n13\nextraHeadsetRangeOutdoor\n—\n—\n80 on the same three weapons.\n✅bench (correlation)\n\n\n14\nfire interval / charge time (ms)\n100\n1250\nProven by one-field flip: a sniper with t14=1250 fired exactly one shot per second. Stock cadences: burst 75 · SMG 90 · AR 100 · sniper 300 · AMR 360 · launcher 360 · shotgun 900 · melee 1000 · rail gun 1200 · charge rifle 1250. For charge weapons this is the hold time.\n✅bench\n\n\n15\n—\n850\n850\n— (unknown)\n—\n\n\n16\nmaxClip\n32\n100\nMagazine size.\n✅bench\n\n\n17\nmaxAmmo\n32768\n32768\nAlways  in captured frames (or 32768 as an unlimited flag). Not an independent knob.\n✅bench (correlation)\n\n\n18\nreloadSpeed (ms)\n1400\n2500\nReload time.\n🔍app\n\n\n19\n—\n0\n0\n— (unknown)\n—\n\n\n20\nfire mode\n0\n14\nProven by one-field flip:  full-auto ·  single-shot/bolt ·  burst (cycle in t23) ·  charge, auto-release (tap = weak shot) ·  hold-to-charge, auto-fire (tap = sound only) ·  tap-fire OR charge-release ·  melee.\n✅bench\n\n\n21\nmaxAccuracy\n100\n100\n\n🔍app\n\n\n22\nsingleShotAccuracy\n100\n100\n\n🔍app\n\n\n23\nburstWeaponTime (ms)\n—\n—\nBurst cycle: 275 Burst Rifle, 250 Force Rifle, empty on everything else.\n✅bench\n\n\n24\noverheat (heat per shot)\n0\n14\nSMG 5 · Energy Rifle 6 · Charge Rifle 14 · Plasma Sniper 30. Inert unless t37/t38 are set.\n✅bench\n\n\n25\n—\n—\n—\n— (unknown)\n—\n\n\n26\n—\n—\n—\n— (unknown)\n—\n\n\n27\nprimaryFire_SoundName\nR01\nE03\nFire sound id. A sound, not an identity — Rocket Launcher and Rail Gun both fire  with different stat lines.\n✅bench\n\n\n28\nextra action sound A\n—\nC15\nEngage sound.  ids = charge (rail gun C08, laser cannon C11, charge rifle C15);  ids = extra reload parts on five-part reloads (sniper/AMR/force rifle D20, ion sniper D32).\n✅bench\n\n\n29\nextra action sound B\n—\nC17\nRelease sound. Present exactly when the weapon has a distinct release event (charge rifle C17, bolt weapons D19/D31); absent on auto-firing chargers.\n✅bench\n\n\n30\nsecondary_Mix_SoundName\n—\n—\n\n🔍app\n\n\n31\nreloadPart1_SoundName\nD04\nD30\n\n✅bench\n\n\n32\nreloadPart2_SoundName\nD03\nD29\n\n✅bench\n\n\n33\nreloadPart3_SoundName\nD02\nD37\n\n✅bench\n\n\n34\nnoAmmo_SoundName\nD18\nA73\n\n🔍app\n\n\n35\nweaponFeatureA\n—\nC19\nOverheat sound (SMG D11, CR C19, Plasma Sniper/Energy Rifle D122).\n✅bench\n\n\n36\nweaponFeatureB\n—\nC04\nSecond feature sound.\n🔍app\n\n\n37\noverheat param A\n—\n20\nGate for the overheat system (with t38): transplanting  onto the SMG brought its dead heat gauge alive and the trigger locked at the top.\n✅bench (gate)\n\n\n38\noverheat param B\n—\n150\nSee t37.\n✅bench (gate)\n\n\n39\nclipStartingAmmo\n32\n100\nEquals t16 in every captured frame.\n✅bench (correlation)\n\n\n40\nammoReserv\n9999999\n9999999\nReserve; 9999999 = unlimited.  in stock frames.\n🔍app\n\n\n41\n—\n75\n75\n— (unknown)\n—\n\n\n42\nextraHeadsetRangeIndoor\n—\n—\n30/30/40 on the three t1=2 weapons.\n✅bench (correlation)\n\n\nSource: protocol/callsign-extract/protocol-classes.md (WEAP exact token positions + cap14–cap24 sections), protocol/brx-protocol.md §6.1 and the t20 / overheat sections, docs/experiment-log.md (2026-08-26 $WEAP token probes; charge modes; overheat solved)\nTwo positions that bit us.(1) The metadata's field order has  before ; the wire has the rate at t14 and the constant 850 at t15 — a compiler that trusted the field order shipped every weapon at 10 shots/s. (2) Keying weapons by their fire sound (t27) silently merges distinct weapons.Source: protocol/brx-protocol.md §6.1; protocol/callsign-extract/protocol-classes.md (cap17, cap18)\nStock weapon signatures(fire sound → weapon → behaviour, as named by the operator at capture)\n\n\nt27\nWeapon\nFire mode / notes\n\n\n\n\nAssault Rifle\nfull auto\n\n\n\nBurst Rifle\n3-round burst (t20=9, t23=275)\n\n\n\nForce Rifle\n3-round burst (t23=250), five-part reload\n\n\n\nBolt Rifle\nsingle shot; carries no t28/t29\n\n\n\nSMG\nfull auto, overheat mechanic (t24=5)\n\n\n\nSuppressor\nfull auto, quiet, no muzzle flash (t25=2, t26=50)\n\n\n\nStinger\nfull auto\n\n\n\nEnergy Rifle\nfull auto, overheat (t24=6), 300-round clip\n\n\n\nSniper\nsingle shot, bolt action (t28/t29 = D20/D19)\n\n\n\nAMR\nsingle shot, same bolt pair\n\n\n\nIon Sniper\nsingle shot, 2-round clip (D32/D31)\n\n\n\nPlasma Sniper\nsingle shot, overheat (t24=30), shell reload\n\n\n\nShotgun\nsingle shot (t20=7), t19=2, extra-headset block, magnitude 45\n\n\n\nEnergy Launcher\nclip 1 / reserve 3\n\n\n\nRail Gun\ncharges on hold, auto-fires ~1.2 s (t20=2, t28=C08)\n\n\n\nRocket Launcher\nsingle shot, protocol 10, magnitude 115\n\n\n\nLaser Cannon\nmust be held (t20=3, t28=C11)\n\n\n\nCharge Rifle\nhold, fires on release; overheats (t20=14)\n\n\n\nMelee\ngyro swing, protocol 13, magnitude 90\n\n\nSource: protocol/callsign-extract/protocol-classes.md (weapon signatures, cap14–cap22); docs/experiment-log.md (2026-08-26 melee capture, damage bench)\nOverheat is a balance lever on any weapon.Set t24 (heat per shot) + t35 (overheat sound) + t37/t38 (enable/params, stock ), and the live heat gauge streams in  token 5 — climbing ~8/shot on the Charge Rifle, crossing 100 into lockout and decaying on idle. A HUD heat bar needs no new protocol.Source: protocol/brx-protocol.md §7j, overheat section; docs/experiment-log.md (overheat mechanism solved)\nCan I build a semi-auto rifle?Yes — t20=7 is single-shot per pull. (An earlier note that semi-auto \"may not exist\" predates the t20 proof.)\nWhat bounds a custom weapon?The firmware's behaviour vocabulary: the DamageType and PowerType enums, ReloadType, six slots, and the 2166 sound ids. Any combination with arbitrary numbers is buildable; a brand-new damage behaviour is not.\nDoes a  re-push mid-game keep the ammo count?No — it resets mag/reserve to the frame's values. Re-send .\nSource: protocol/brx-protocol.md t20 section · protocol/callsign-extract/protocol-classes.md (\"What's moddable\") · docs/gotchas.md\n\n\n  "}},"afterSnapshot":"after@call@266"}
